// FRAGMENT — paste this inside the existing
//   match /databases/{database}/documents { ... }
// block, next to the other matches. Do not deploy this file by itself.
// It is not a complete ruleset. The live rules file is not in this
// repository. The owner publishes rules separately. Do not deploy until
// the owner approves.
//
// jobCosting holds manager-only site days (Lexington Club, Aspen, and any
// other whole-crew day with no route stops) and the break-even setting.
// Docs:
//   settings          { kind:'settings', dailyOverhead, truckCount, updatedAt, updatedBy }
//   sd_*              { kind:'siteDay', propId, propertyName, date, crewId, hours, people, trucks, createdAt, updatedBy }
//
// Crew phones must not read this collection. It is not pay, but it is a
// manager screen and the property names here can include jobs that are
// not on a crew route.
//
// isManager() is the existing helper (verified manager email).

match /jobCosting/{docId} {
  allow read, create, update, delete: if isManager();
}

// propertyPrivate already stores monthlyRate for the manager. This screen
// also saves two optional fields on the same doc:
//   budgetHoursPerVisit, budgetCrewSize
// If the live propertyPrivate match lets the manager write the document
// without a field allow-list, no change is required. If it uses
// hasOnly([...]), add those two keys to the list. Crew still cannot read
// propertyPrivate.

// arrivedAtISO is a new field on a route stop. Crew write it with the same
// routes/{id} update they already use to complete a stop (saveAndSync).
// If the live route rule allows that update for any signed-in crew, no
// change is required. If it allow-lists stop fields, add arrivedAtISO next
// to completedAtISO and navigateTappedAtISO.
